     8	    Create a function that takes a value (string) representing a number
     9	    and returns the closest integer to it. If the number is equidistant
    10	    from two integers, round it away from zero.
    11	
    12	    Examples
    13	    >>> closest_integer("10")
    14	    10
    15	    >>> closest_integer("15.3")
    16	    15
    17	
    18	    Note:
    19	    Rounding away from zero means that if the given number is equidistant
    20	    from two integers, the one you should return is the one that is the
    21	    farthest from zero. For example closest_integer("14.5") should
    22	    return 15 and closest_integer("-14.5") should return -15.
    23	    '''
    24	    from math import floor, ceil
    25	
    26	    if value.count('.') == 1:
    27	        # remove trailing zeros
